WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.175 --> 00:00:02.138
- Thank You, Economy
is my last audio book.

00:00:02.138 --> 00:00:03.039
- [DRock] When was that?

00:00:03.039 --> 00:00:05.285
- 2011, probably recorded it in

00:00:05.285 --> 00:00:08.405
December 2010.

00:00:08.405 --> 00:00:09.973
(whooshing)

00:00:09.973 --> 00:00:12.389
(thumping)

00:00:12.389 --> 00:00:15.039
(upbeat music)

00:00:15.039 --> 00:00:17.459
- I really don't have a
mindset on social media.

00:00:17.459 --> 00:00:19.214
I do things, I look at things from

00:00:19.214 --> 00:00:20.945
this lens that

00:00:20.945 --> 00:00:22.110
I'm doing something fun and cool

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:23.225
and I find it interesting,

00:00:23.225 --> 00:00:24.651
and I want to share it, I share it.

00:00:24.651 --> 00:00:26.568
I'm usually of the nature of

00:00:26.568 --> 00:00:28.723
being more private than anything,

00:00:28.723 --> 00:00:31.624
but seriously.
(laughing)

00:00:31.624 --> 00:00:34.167
Some people, and obviously
it's going to be you,

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.886
I've always been told
people just want to see

00:00:35.886 --> 00:00:38.608
just the dumbest things that you're doing.

00:00:38.608 --> 00:00:39.875
You may not find it interesting,

00:00:39.875 --> 00:00:41.674
but everybody else finds it interesting

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.878
just because it's a lens
into your world, and whatnot.

00:00:43.878 --> 00:00:46.109
So, I'm getting a little bit
more comfortable with that.

00:00:46.109 --> 00:00:46.975
- And just so you know,

00:00:46.975 --> 00:00:48.015
just so I keep aligning things,

00:00:48.015 --> 00:00:50.277
and I'll get more detailed
about this in '16,

00:00:50.277 --> 00:00:55.172
I don't not believe in anything.

00:00:55.172 --> 00:00:56.530
Thank you so much.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:59.902
- [DRock] You're welcome.

00:00:59.902 --> 00:01:02.102
Have a good day.
- [Gary] You too.

00:01:02.102 --> 00:01:06.647
(pulsing music)

00:01:09.211 --> 00:01:10.784
- [Gary] Yes sir.

00:01:10.784 --> 00:01:14.996
Ready to star in some DailyVee action?

00:01:14.996 --> 00:01:16.200
- Oh, boy.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.446
(laughing)

00:01:17.446 --> 00:01:18.924
- He's funny to edit

00:01:18.924 --> 00:01:20.061
because I have to wa--

00:01:20.061 --> 00:01:21.397
I mean, I never watch anything

00:01:21.397 --> 00:01:23.000
of my own stuff ever before,

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.382
but I have to watch this.

00:01:24.382 --> 00:01:25.924
There's just so much.

00:01:25.924 --> 00:01:27.282
- [Jason] Right, and I
can see you sitting down.

00:01:27.282 --> 00:01:28.444
- It was like that part--

00:01:28.444 --> 00:01:29.662
Like, literally, I got to
that point and I was like,

00:01:29.662 --> 00:01:30.742
I'm going to leave that in there,

00:01:30.742 --> 00:01:32.182
because I think Jason's going to watch it.

00:01:32.182 --> 00:01:33.100
(laughing)

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:34.353
I'm hoping he's going to be like,

00:01:34.353 --> 00:01:35.281
what did he say?

00:01:35.281 --> 00:01:36.942
Because, for me it was easy.

00:01:36.942 --> 00:01:38.241
I was going up against something

00:01:38.241 --> 00:01:39.623
where I would market,

00:01:39.623 --> 00:01:41.238
and then I would see it come through

00:01:41.238 --> 00:01:42.933
the dot com shopping cart,

00:01:42.933 --> 00:01:45.381
or my register in the store.

00:01:45.381 --> 00:01:47.238
So, I never had to debate

00:01:47.238 --> 00:01:48.539
the things that you have to debate.

00:01:48.539 --> 00:01:49.839
The big shock to me

00:01:49.839 --> 00:01:51.940
when I came into corporate America

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.821
was reporting.

00:01:53.821 --> 00:01:55.144
Millward Brown,

00:01:55.144 --> 00:01:57.199
Neilson's brand list.

00:01:57.199 --> 00:01:58.928
Even the stuff that's been
beneficial to our business,

00:01:58.928 --> 00:02:00.078
DataLogics.

00:02:00.078 --> 00:02:02.342
Just reporting.

00:02:02.342 --> 00:02:06.364
(hip hop music)

00:02:06.364 --> 00:02:07.861
You know, for me,

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:09.207
when I do business meetings,

00:02:09.207 --> 00:02:10.425
it's kind of interesting,

00:02:10.425 --> 00:02:14.444
I just so know where my
intent and my skills are,

00:02:14.444 --> 00:02:17.345
that I actually--not judge,

00:02:17.345 --> 00:02:21.281
but I size up the other side

00:02:21.281 --> 00:02:23.499
based on how they react to me.

00:02:23.499 --> 00:02:24.822
Because if it goes well,

00:02:24.822 --> 00:02:26.203
it means they're seeing what I'm saying,

00:02:26.203 --> 00:02:27.922
there's a belief on the--

00:02:27.922 --> 00:02:29.501
there's an alignment on the religion.

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:30.882
You've got to back it up now.

00:02:30.882 --> 00:02:33.865
But I want to put myself on the hook,

00:02:33.865 --> 00:02:36.501
and I'm always so thankful
when very senior people

00:02:36.501 --> 00:02:40.261
are not posturing to the history,

00:02:40.261 --> 00:02:41.655
they're open-minded,

00:02:41.655 --> 00:02:44.104
they're bringing their strong
points of view as well.

00:02:44.104 --> 00:02:46.415
But it's like a fair debate,

00:02:46.415 --> 00:02:48.620
it's honest, it lacks emotion,

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:50.001
it's just business,

00:02:50.001 --> 00:02:52.661
and it's just a great
way to get the day going.

00:02:52.661 --> 00:02:55.040
To have an invigorating, high-level,

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:57.281
important meeting.

00:02:57.281 --> 00:02:59.080
That was fair.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.194
And, by the way,

00:03:00.194 --> 00:03:01.402
if I don't get any business

00:03:01.402 --> 00:03:02.597
or if my business doesn't grow,

00:03:02.597 --> 00:03:03.654
and I felt that was fair,

00:03:03.654 --> 00:03:05.302
and that's happened in the past,

00:03:05.302 --> 00:03:06.520
because I don't think what I do

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.100
or what we do aligns with them,

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.273
I also feel good.

00:03:09.273 --> 00:03:10.561
It's not about the win,

00:03:10.561 --> 00:03:14.342
it's about the fairness.

00:03:14.342 --> 00:03:17.058
Meritocracy, baby.

00:03:17.058 --> 00:03:18.556
Even at your own expense,

00:03:18.556 --> 00:03:20.379
something that a lot of
people haven't learned yet.

00:03:20.379 --> 00:03:23.992
♫ Harm anybody who ridin' against

00:03:23.992 --> 00:03:27.040
♫ She said you done had a long day, baby

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.001
♫ Let me get up on top

00:03:29.001 --> 00:03:32.146
♫ She know I'm a winner, yeah

00:03:32.146 --> 00:03:34.202
♫ She know I'm a winner

00:03:34.202 --> 00:03:37.660
♫ I'm'a figure how to get up on top

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:39.341
♫ Okay, okay

00:03:39.341 --> 00:03:41.039
♫ I'm a Ponce de León

00:03:41.039 --> 00:03:42.618
♫ What you want ♫

00:03:42.618 --> 00:03:44.801
- That's fine, or, or, or

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:46.274
maybe I could see her over the weekend

00:03:46.274 --> 00:03:48.144
if she wants to stop by and see the kids.

00:03:48.144 --> 00:03:49.201
Because she's a family friend

00:03:49.201 --> 00:03:54.201
with Dave, so ask, okay?

00:03:55.137 --> 00:03:58.573
Okay, okay, bye.

00:03:58.573 --> 00:04:00.297
(muttering)

00:04:00.297 --> 00:04:01.556
- [Rick] Hi there, Gary.

00:04:01.556 --> 00:04:02.497
- Gary.

00:04:02.497 --> 00:04:04.737
The nice thing is, I'm excited is that,

00:04:04.737 --> 00:04:06.199
the questions are already read

00:04:06.199 --> 00:04:09.079
so it's going to be interesting to see.

00:04:09.079 --> 00:04:10.541
- [Rick] We'll put you on headphones.

00:04:10.541 --> 00:04:11.876
You'll hear the questions,

00:04:11.876 --> 00:04:13.642
we'll be able to play
the questions for you.

00:04:13.642 --> 00:04:16.394
- It's huge, and you know what's crazy?

00:04:16.394 --> 00:04:18.296
I have a crazy idea.

00:04:18.296 --> 00:04:19.726
You know what's interesting?

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:22.429
You want to talk about

00:04:22.429 --> 00:04:23.751
why the audio book?

00:04:23.751 --> 00:04:24.680
(grunting)

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:25.636
Okay, cool, I'm excited.

00:04:25.636 --> 00:04:27.156
I think this is going
to go really well, yeah.

00:04:27.156 --> 00:04:29.073
What's better than uh,

00:04:29.073 --> 00:04:30.792
you know what's actually really rad?

00:04:30.792 --> 00:04:32.114
How did I answer to the book,

00:04:32.114 --> 00:04:33.612
and how did I answer in the audio book?

00:04:33.612 --> 00:04:35.412
Like what little, subtle things changed

00:04:35.412 --> 00:04:38.742
in a three or four month period?

00:04:38.742 --> 00:04:41.216
I mean, if I could just sit
and just answer questions

00:04:41.216 --> 00:04:45.086
I'd be done in four seconds.

00:04:45.086 --> 00:04:47.071
- [Rick] Come on in.

00:04:47.071 --> 00:04:48.290
Cozy, worth it.

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:49.370
Few studios in New York City

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:50.717
that has a window.

00:04:50.717 --> 00:04:51.679
(laughing)

00:04:51.679 --> 00:04:52.678
So you can be there

00:04:52.678 --> 00:04:54.610
with a little human light in this place.

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:56.142
Which is, so always good.

00:04:56.142 --> 00:04:57.114
- Let me take a second
and catch up on my life,

00:04:57.114 --> 00:05:00.263
give me a second.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:05.581
- [Rick] Getting the iPad.

00:05:05.581 --> 00:05:07.520
- [DRock] What is the last audio book?

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:08.681
Thank You, Ecocomy, right?

00:05:08.681 --> 00:05:10.619
- Thank You Economy
is my last audio book.

00:05:10.619 --> 00:05:11.920
- [DRock] When was that?

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:13.869
- 2011.

00:05:13.869 --> 00:05:15.844
I think it came out on March '11,

00:05:15.844 --> 00:05:20.325
so I probably recorded
it in December 2010.

00:05:20.325 --> 00:05:23.374
(chuckling)

00:05:23.374 --> 00:05:24.998
So that's one thing that changed

00:05:24.998 --> 00:05:27.446
since five years ago,
when I did my last book.

00:05:27.446 --> 00:05:28.464
- No more paper.

00:05:28.464 --> 00:05:29.915
I don't know if you're going to need this,

00:05:29.915 --> 00:05:31.308
you may not want it,

00:05:31.308 --> 00:05:32.689
but that's a list of the questions

00:05:32.689 --> 00:05:33.943
and who's asking them,

00:05:33.943 --> 00:05:35.590
and the order in which they come up.

00:05:35.590 --> 00:05:37.251
- This is so cool how he did it.

00:05:37.251 --> 00:05:38.424
- You'll want this page,

00:05:38.424 --> 00:05:40.513
so that people will say
all sorts of things.

00:05:40.513 --> 00:05:42.174
- Like this, like literally
everything that's on the page?

00:05:42.174 --> 00:05:43.904
- Yeah, well, not all of them.

00:05:43.904 --> 00:05:45.065
- Got it.
(chuckling)

00:05:45.065 --> 00:05:46.249
- Maybe you'll leave an open question.

00:05:46.249 --> 00:05:47.132
But--

00:05:47.132 --> 00:05:50.209
(muttering)

00:05:50.209 --> 00:05:52.734
A little later there's
a Missy Elliot lyric.

00:05:52.734 --> 00:05:54.219
You can't sing.

00:05:54.219 --> 00:05:54.940
- I won't.

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:56.439
- That's not an evaluation.

00:05:56.439 --> 00:05:59.109
(laughing)

00:05:59.109 --> 00:06:00.923
- People are actually reading questions

00:06:00.923 --> 00:06:04.754
and I'm answering them in the book.

00:06:11.478 --> 00:06:16.478
- Alright, so we're anticipating

00:06:16.802 --> 00:06:19.880
some improvisation here, yes?

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:21.261
But let's try reading,

00:06:21.261 --> 00:06:22.956
obviously you want to read the credits.

00:06:22.956 --> 00:06:23.942
- I'm going to read, yeah,

00:06:23.942 --> 00:06:25.463
there's an opening setups we will read,

00:06:25.463 --> 00:06:29.677
and then when I was reading it myself,

00:06:29.677 --> 00:06:32.441
it was funny how I was,

00:06:32.441 --> 00:06:33.857
there was something interesting going on,

00:06:33.857 --> 00:06:37.038
which is, I improv'd

00:06:37.038 --> 00:06:40.764
eight to 13 percent in my first two books.

00:06:40.764 --> 00:06:44.222
Here, I could see going a lot more.

00:06:44.222 --> 00:06:46.243
Okay, this is now from
a business standpoint,

00:06:46.243 --> 00:06:48.915
there is an absolute scenario here

00:06:48.915 --> 00:06:51.572
where a lot of people could end up

00:06:51.572 --> 00:06:53.615
buying both the book and the audio book

00:06:53.615 --> 00:06:56.100
if I make them aware that I basically--

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:57.179
- That there's a difference.

00:06:57.179 --> 00:06:58.316
There's more value.

00:06:58.316 --> 00:07:00.778
- Some of these answers
I gave a year and--

00:07:00.778 --> 00:07:03.274
By the way, some of them I saw

00:07:03.274 --> 00:07:05.039
and things changed even when

00:07:05.039 --> 00:07:06.339
I couldn't change them anymore.

00:07:06.339 --> 00:07:07.778
- Like Andy Dalton.

00:07:07.778 --> 00:07:12.038
(laughing)
- [Gary] Very good.

00:07:12.038 --> 00:07:14.814
- You've got a lot of material to do,

00:07:14.814 --> 00:07:16.137
we've got a lot to do,

00:07:16.137 --> 00:07:18.412
there's only one cardinal rule.

00:07:18.412 --> 00:07:19.573
Don't rush.

00:07:19.573 --> 00:07:20.977
You've got to listen to the audio

00:07:20.977 --> 00:07:23.393
that was up on Audible for the last book.

00:07:23.393 --> 00:07:24.773
Sounded perfect.

00:07:24.773 --> 00:07:27.711
The pace was great, you weren't rushing,

00:07:27.711 --> 00:07:30.996
the big temptation is to push too fast.

00:07:30.996 --> 00:07:32.958
Pull back, relax.

00:07:32.958 --> 00:07:35.036
- I feel very good about the
time that we've allocated.

00:07:35.036 --> 00:07:37.335
I think, in general, you'll
see that I'll probably

00:07:37.335 --> 00:07:38.949
start a little bit too hard,

00:07:38.949 --> 00:07:41.433
because I'm excited, but cool.

00:07:41.433 --> 00:07:43.035
- [Rick] Gary, can you hear me?

00:07:43.035 --> 00:07:44.253
- I can hear you perfectly.

00:07:44.253 --> 00:07:45.415
- [Rick] Great, thank you.

00:07:45.415 --> 00:07:47.552
The wonderful moments.

00:07:47.552 --> 00:07:50.255
Alright, so what I ask for getting levels

00:07:50.255 --> 00:07:51.707
and things of that sort.

00:07:51.707 --> 00:07:53.913
To the Vayniacs, it's the first,

00:07:53.913 --> 00:07:55.712
it's the dedication if you will.

00:07:55.712 --> 00:07:56.768
- Before we do the--

00:07:56.768 --> 00:07:58.474
- [Rick] Just because that's not going

00:07:58.474 --> 00:07:59.474
to give us enough say.

00:07:59.474 --> 00:08:01.214
So, let me hear you read that,

00:08:01.214 --> 00:08:04.521
and we'll get a level, go.

00:08:04.521 --> 00:08:06.842
- To the Vayniacs and the Vayner Nation,

00:08:06.842 --> 00:08:08.561
and all the people who have watched

00:08:08.561 --> 00:08:11.939
even one video over the last ten years,

00:08:11.939 --> 00:08:15.421
your attention is my oxygen.

00:08:15.421 --> 00:08:17.418
Harper Audio presents

00:08:17.418 --> 00:08:19.879
#AskGaryVee, One Entrepreneur's Take

00:08:19.879 --> 00:08:23.397
on Leadership, Social
Media, and Self-Awareness,

00:08:23.397 --> 00:08:27.460
by Gary Vaynerchuk.

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:30.502
Sometimes you get emotional
at some of these things.

00:08:30.502 --> 00:08:32.313
Do I say the word acknowledgements?

00:08:32.313 --> 00:08:33.461
- [Rick] Yeah.

00:08:33.461 --> 00:08:35.134
- Acknowledgements.

00:08:35.134 --> 00:08:38.501
Nothing I do is possible without
the support of my family.

00:08:38.501 --> 00:08:40.447
My heart belongs to my wife Lizzie,

00:08:40.447 --> 00:08:42.419
and my kids Misha and Xander.

00:08:42.419 --> 00:08:44.440
At the time I really did think I was done

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:47.563
with daily video blogging forever.

00:08:47.563 --> 00:08:49.884
I could imagine the occasional interview

00:08:49.884 --> 00:08:51.219
or one-off video.

00:08:51.219 --> 00:08:52.706
Have you seen my Monday morning

00:08:52.706 --> 00:08:54.262
motivational spot?

00:08:54.262 --> 00:08:56.479
But a full show was too much.

00:08:56.479 --> 00:08:58.428
There was only one
thing I didn't count on,

00:08:58.428 --> 00:09:00.088
you, the Vayner Nation.

00:09:00.088 --> 00:09:01.225
I missed you.

00:09:01.225 --> 00:09:03.526
Meanwhile, the e-mails kept pouring in.

00:09:03.526 --> 00:09:06.706
Despite access to three
books and hundreds of videos,

00:09:06.706 --> 00:09:08.599
people still had questions;

00:09:08.599 --> 00:09:10.839
How to successfully use social media,

00:09:10.839 --> 00:09:13.622
the new platforms, and the old standbys?

00:09:13.622 --> 00:09:14.922
To build their brands,

00:09:14.922 --> 00:09:17.674
or how to market with native content,

00:09:17.674 --> 00:09:20.553
or even just how do I do what I do?

00:09:20.553 --> 00:09:22.642
There was so much content, I would--

00:09:22.642 --> 00:09:24.419
There was so much content I

00:09:24.419 --> 00:09:26.276
wanted to put out to help them,

00:09:26.276 --> 00:09:27.913
but with all my other obligations

00:09:27.913 --> 00:09:29.619
at VaynerMedia and elsewhere,

00:09:29.619 --> 00:09:32.034
I just couldn't get to it.

00:09:32.034 --> 00:09:35.656
And that's how on July 31st 2014,

00:09:35.656 --> 00:09:39.080
on a YouTube channel
with 30,000 subscribers,

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:40.938
one of the world's first business

00:09:40.938 --> 00:09:43.515
Q and A video blogs was launched.

00:09:43.515 --> 00:09:45.895
It opened with a guy in
a blue-striped golf shirt

00:09:45.895 --> 00:09:47.578
smiling into the camera.

00:09:47.578 --> 00:09:48.774
Hello, everybody and--

00:09:48.774 --> 00:09:52.131
Oh, I forgot my own intro.
(laughing)

00:09:52.131 --> 00:09:53.351
Hello everyone,

00:09:53.351 --> 00:09:56.301
and welcome to the first #AskGaryVee.

00:09:56.301 --> 00:09:57.846
Though the first episode started off

00:09:57.846 --> 00:10:01.305
almost as low-key as its
wine themed predecessors,

00:10:01.305 --> 00:10:04.068
by the second the light
and the sound quality

00:10:04.068 --> 00:10:05.368
were professional grade,

00:10:05.368 --> 00:10:07.725
and the host was bringing hard energy

00:10:07.725 --> 00:10:09.790
and straight thunder.

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:11.369
At first I thought the show might be an

00:10:11.369 --> 00:10:13.829
every now and then thing,

00:10:13.829 --> 00:10:15.607
but it was like riding a bike.

00:10:15.607 --> 00:10:17.360
As soon as I filmed the first episode

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:18.786
I wanted to do more.

